{"name":"Babbling Creek","hex":"#a7bad3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"babbling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a stage in child language acquisition, during which an infant appears to be experimenting with uttering sounds of language, but not yet producing any recognizable words","sounds produced by infant during the babbling period"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That babbles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/babbling"},{"term":"creek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small inlet, often saltwater, leading to the sea or to the main channel of a river, especially a river estuary.","The inner part of a port that is used as a dock for small boats."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Babbling","blocks":[{"text":"Babbling is a stage in child development and a state in language acquisition during which an infant appears to be experimenting with uttering articulate sounds, but does not yet produce any recognizable words. Babbling begins shortly after birth and progresses through several stages as the infant's repertoire of sounds expands and vocalizations become more speech-like. Infants typically begin to produce recognizable words when they are around 12 months of age, though babbling may continue for some time afterward."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Infant_babbling_in_crib.ogv/330px--Infant_babbling_in_crib.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babbling","wikidata":"Q1723890"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"creek":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/39/En-us-creek.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/39/En-us-creek.ogg/En-us-creek.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikiped